ttable family as they endure years of sacrifice and separation, willing themselves out of shantytown poverty into a new global middle class. At the heart of the story is Tita's daughter, Rosalie. Beating the odds, she struggles through nursing school and works her way across the Middle East until a Texas hospital fulfills her dreams with a job offer in the States.","pageCount":402,"publicationYear":2019,"subjectCategories":[{"source":"google_books","scheme":"google_books_category","label":"History","sourceId":"source-google-books-summary-a-good-provider-is-one-who-leaves-one-family-and-migration-in-the-21st-century-jason-deparle"}],"displaySummary":"When Jason DeParle moved into the Manila slums with Tita Comodas and her family three decades ago, he never imagined his reporting on them would span three generations and turn into the defining chronicle of a new age--the age of global migration. In a monumental book that gives new meaning to \"immersion journalism,\" DeParle paints an intimate portrait of an unforgettable family as they endure years of sacrifice and separation, willing themselves out of shantytown poverty into a new global middle class. At the heart of the story is Tita's daughter, Rosalie. Beating the odds, she struggles through nursing school and works her way across the Middle East until a Texas hospital fulfills her dreams with a job offer in the States.","primaryTopic":"Immigration, Refugees & Borderlands","subjectEvidence":{"primarySubject":"Race & Ethnicity","confidence":"medium","method":"evidence_score","candidates":[{"subject":"Race & Ethnicity","score":8,"evidenceCount":1}],"evidence":[{"source":"llm_classifier","rawLabel":"Race & Ethnicity","mappedSubject":"Race & Ethnicity","score":8,"confidence":"high","note":"The book primarily focuses on migration, which is closely related to themes of race and ethnicity, while also offering a rich narrative through immersive journalism that explores societal impacts.","id":"subject-evidence-book-a-good